[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"GitHub API Integration, Custom Webhooks, and Status Checks in GitHub Actions"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Automating your development workflow often requires extending beyond native GitHub Actions. By integrating the GitHub REST API, handling incoming webhooks via custom servers, and reporting programmatic status checks, you can build powerful, tightly integrated CI/CD pipelines."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Authentication"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To interact with the GitHub API inside a workflow, you must authenticate. GitHub Actions automatically generates a GITHUB_TOKEN secret for every run, which can be granted specific permissions in your workflow configuration."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"name: API Integration Workflow
on: [push]
permissions:
  contents: read
  statuses: write
  pull-requests: write
jobs:
  api-call:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Call GitHub API
        uses: actions/github-script@v6
        with:
          script: |
            const response = await github.rest.repos.get({
              owner: context.repo.owner,
              repo: context.repo.repo,
            });
            console.log("Repository description: " + response.data.description);"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Setting Up Custom Webhooks"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Webhooks allow external services to be notified when certain events happen on GitHub. You can configure webhooks at the repository or organization level to point to your custom endpoint receiver."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Navigate to your repository Settings -> Webhooks -> Add webhook."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Provide your Payload URL and select 'application/json' as the content type."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Set a secure secret token to validate incoming payloads and prevent spoofing."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Choose individual events or select 'Send me everything'."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"const express = require('express');
const crypto = require('crypto');
const app = express();

app.use(express.json());

app.post('/webhook', (req, res) => {
  const signature = req.headers['x-hub-signature-256'];
  const payload = JSON.stringify(req.body);
  const secret = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;

  const hmac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret);
  const digest = 'sha256=' + hmac.update(payload).digest('hex');

  if (signature === digest) {
    console.log('Verified webhook event:', req.headers['x-github-event']);
    res.status(200).send('Webhook received successfully');
  } else {
    res.status(401).send('Signature mismatch');
  }
});

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Server running on port 3000'));"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Reporting Commit Status Checks"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Status checks allow you to integrate external testing tools and build results directly into the GitHub pull request interface. You can set states such as pending, success, failure, or error."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"name: Report Status Check
on: [push]
jobs:
  status:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Set Pending Status
        uses: actions/github-script@v6
        with:
          script: |
            await github.rest.repos.createCommitStatus({
              owner: context.repo.owner,
              repo: context.repo.repo,
              sha: context.sha,
              state: 'pending',
              description: 'Running custom quality checks...',
              context: 'ci/quality-gate'
            });
      - name: Perform Check
        run: echo "Running tests..."
      - name: Set Success Status
        if: success()
        uses: actions/github-script@v6
        with:
          script: |
            await github.rest.repos.createCommitStatus({
              owner: context.repo.owner,
              repo: context.repo.repo,
              sha: context.sha,
              state: 'success',
              description: 'Quality checks passed!',
              context: 'ci/quality-gate'
            });"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining GitHub API interactions, listening to custom webhooks, and dynamically updating commit statuses, you unlock limitless capabilities for extending GitHub Actions into a truly bespoke deployment and monitoring pipeline."}]
